From 2cf83e9311d5c165f230483466994f819d334dae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 09:54:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fixture: reconcile wall areas with their own dimensions

garage-house.json contradicted itself twice: five of six wall faces had
area_mm2 5-18% off from width x height (+ gable), and four stored net
areas were 26 sq ft below gross minus that wall's own openings. The
widths come from the footprint and the heights from the eave height -
both documented building values - so the stored areas were the wrong
side. Recomputed area_mm2 = w*h + 0.5*w*gable and net = area minus the
openings attributed via parent_face_id. All six walls now pass the 2%
consistency check in berechnung.ts.

Golden value moves with it: walls net 2,682 -> 2,779 sq ft (test and
docs/plan.md). Roof, openings and downspouts are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014xT2L4T9xXoRRGon2pZcKX
